# VFX Harness core rules

The harness is a control system and an agent-capability product. Model judgment proposes;
typed contracts, evidence, checkpoints, and replay accept. Making agents smarter is a
first-class goal: instruments, bounded unit context, tool policy, and closed loops — not
larger prompts, and not model confidence as acceptance.

- Read `AGENTS.md` and the relevant `docs/architecture`, ADR, HIR, and tests first.
- Follow `docs/operations/improvement-lifecycle.md` for pain points and behavior changes.
- Follow `docs/operations/running-vfx-harness.md` to run or diagnose a shot.
- Read run metadata in order: latest pointer → manifest → status → summary → artifact index.
- Never write or read evidence from shot-root legacy output directories.
- Treat model output as a proposal; authoritative contracts and replay decide acceptance.
- Keep domain code independent of Claude SDK, Blender, network, filesystem, and eval fixtures.
- Parallelize evidence production; serialize authoritative mutation and integration.
- Do not add shot names, fixed shot frames, display-name selectors, or scene coordinates to core code.
- Do not patch a single render when the failure reveals a reusable harness capability.
- Core behavior changes require root-cause evidence, regression coverage, and an HIR update.
- Preserve unrelated and uncommitted user work.
